  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As we move from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> we are moving from high potential to low potential. Since <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is connected to +<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> terminal of battery it should be at a positive potential. <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> is grounded hence it should be at zero potential. <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> should be at a negative potential.",
